  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Simultaneous Linear Equations",
    "description": "Solve two- and three-equation systems that appear inside simplification questions, including cost puzzles and one simple quadratic.",
    "teachingApproach": "Start with a cost story whose equations add up kindly, then build: scaling before subtracting, ratio-plus-linear systems, three-equation reduction, the pure scaling shortcut, a factor-pair quadratic, a fractional word system, and the half-ticket capstone. Every system ends with a substitution check, and every idea gets a fresh question plus a parallel retry.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 4, Simplification. Approved scope: Teach elimination for two equations: adding or subtracting to remove a variable, as in 4 bags + 3 boxes = ₹555 with 3 bags + 4 boxes = ₹460 where adding gives x + y directly. Cover systems needing one equation scaled first, ratio forms such as 3x/2y = 21/22 converted to x/y before combining with 4x + 5y = 83, and three-equation systems solved by pairwise subtraction. Include the scaling pattern where 4 rings + 2 bangles = ₹57200 gives 6 rings + 3 bangles without finding single prices, and the book's simple quadratic x^2 − 7x = −12 solved by spotting factor pairs, reporting both roots. Include a two-statement word system (marks in two subjects) and the half-ticket reservation problem. Learners should check solutions by substituting into both original equations and report exactly the quantity asked."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn to solve two puzzles at once.\n\nExams hand you two sentences about the same unknowns — bags and boxes, tickets and reservations. By the end you'll translate both, eliminate cleanly, and check your answer in the original story.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's solve two puzzles at once.\n\n4 bags + 3 boxes cost ₹555.\n3 bags + 4 boxes cost ₹460.\n\nCall a bag x and a box y:\n\n4x + 3y = 555\n3x + 4y = 460",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Here's the gift: add the two equations.\n\n7x + 7y = 1015\nx + y = 145\n\nNow subtract them:\n\nx − y = 95\n\nAdd these two results: 2x = 240, so x = 120.\n\nOne bag costs ₹120.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
