    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Not every pair adds up so kindly:\n\n2x + 3y = 34\nx + y = 13\n\nMake the x's match first. Multiply the second equation by 2:\n\n2x + 2y = 26",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now subtract:\n\n(2x + 3y) − (2x + 2y) = 34 − 26\ny = 8\n\nThen x = 13 − 8 = 5.\n\nAnd if the question asks 5y + 7x: 40 + 35 = 75.\n\nAlways re-read what the question actually wants — often it's not x or y alone.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
